WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.272
Sooner or later, every role changes hands.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.812
Someone writes a note for the next person.

00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:13.082
At Slop University, Dr Iben Chikere studies what those notes keep,

00:00:13.282 --> 00:00:14.242
and what they leave out.

00:00:14.842 --> 00:00:18.558
Most street library volunteers learn the checklist from the last one,

00:00:18.708 --> 00:00:19.858
not the policy.

00:00:20.358 --> 00:00:21.868
When a house is sold,

00:00:22.018 --> 00:00:24.718
the sprinklers keep the old owners' hours.

00:00:25.218 --> 00:00:29.688
And new volunteer officers who ring their predecessor are more likely to stay on.

00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:33.718
No researcher at the University has won more funding than Dr Chikere.

00:00:34.518 --> 00:00:36.188
More than one and a half million dollars.

00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:38.208
And two hundred and nineteen outputs,

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:39.518
the most in her School.

00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:43.278
I've written with all thirty-seven of my colleagues.

00:00:43.578 --> 00:00:45.638
You can't study handovers on your own.

00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:47.548
Look her up on our website,

00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:49.308
follow along on Bluesky,

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:50.178
or leave us a note.
